    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Reading these numbers",
      "id": 16,
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 24
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "**Nothing on this dashboard is a result.** These are live operational values.\nOnly a run recorded under `experiments/results/` supports a reported number.\n\n**The two durations must never be added.** `fleet_recovery_duration_millis`\n(gateway) runs from failure detection to confirmed heartbeats — that is MTTR.\n`fleet_operator_detection_to_replacement_millis` ends when the API server\naccepts the replacement pod; it starts at the same instant and is *already\ncontained* in the gateway's number. Summing them roughly doubles the answer.\n\n**`fleet_devices_known` counts ghosts.** Retained presence outlives the device\nthat set it (ADR-004), so use `fleet_devices_reporting` for fleet size."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Operator: detection to replacement",
      "id": 17,
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "description": "A COMPONENT of MTTR, not MTTR. See the note to the left.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 24
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
